      "id": 16964,
      "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
      "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-08-03T05:32:27.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I wanted to take a moment to admire the fact that even though none of the cards have flavor text (which is a real shame, but there's just no room*) pretty much every card portays it's flavor so perfectly that they don't need any text to accompany them. &nbsp;The art, the evocative titles, and the rules text fill in all the gaps. &nbsp;When Lightning is Shattering Homesteads, it's clear what's going on. &nbsp;When Fangs Preys on the Builders, it's perfectly clear why it's preventing builds. &nbsp;When the Invaders start looking for Scapegoats, or the Island suffers a Year of Little Rain we don't even need art to tie the effects to the flavor. &nbsp;That is really cool.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>* Also, I'm pretty sure that the flavor text on at least half the cards would be variations of \"Ach, Hans, run! &nbsp;It's the ____\" and \"Aiieee!\"</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:49:52.637Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
